{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory contains serious responsibility-chain errors despite many later correct actions. After a suspicious breast pathology result and the patient’s explicit concern about needing breast-surgery follow-up, the doctor advised waiting for online review before determining whether follow-up was needed, and later asserted “没有浸润性成分” before complete pathology was confirmed. These were preventable, actionable errors that could falsely reassure or delay breast-specialist review, so the deterministic boundary is grade 1 even though the final closure became safer and traceable.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00701",
        "explanation": "Final doctor message corrected the residual uncertainty and gave a concrete monitoring/follow-up path.",
        "quote": "最终结果要等完整报告和复诊确认"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00716",
        "explanation": "Patient demonstrated receipt of the corrected bounded plan.",
        "quote": "不能自己说死“肯定没浸润”"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The final bounded episode was closed with a practical plan for checking pathology/supplemental results, when to contact the breast clinic, what documents to bring, and wound red flags. However, this valid final closure does not erase earlier serious responsibility-chain errors.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
